        },
        {
          "line_no": 7,
          "page": 7,
          "start_offset": 216
        }
      ],
      "text": "The ferry came into Low Harbor on the last tide of October, 1871, riding so low that the gulls walked its rail like inspectors. Ada Quill stepped off with a brass theodolite in one hand and a letter of credit in the other, and neither was worth what she had been promised."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line_no": 8,
          "page": 7,
          "start_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "line_no": 9,
          "page": 7,
          "start_offset": 55
        },
        {
          "line_no": 10,
          "page": 7,
          "start_offset": 106
        },
        {
          "line_no": 11,
          "page": 7,
          "start_offset": 163
        },
        {
          "line_no": 12,
          "page": 7,
          "start_offset": 219
        },
        {
          "line_no": 13,
          "page": 7,
          "start_offset": 272
        }
      ],
      "text": "The harbormaster was a narrow man named Osric Penn who kept his ledgers in a biscuit tin. He told her the survey office had closed in the spring and that the nine crowns owed to her were owed, in turn, by a man who had drowned. She thanked him. It was, she said, the most complete account of a debt she had ever received."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line_no": 1,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "line_no": 2,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 55
        },
        {
          "line_no": 3,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 107
        },
        {
          "line_no": 4,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 163
        },
        {
          "line_no": 5,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 214
        },
        {
          "line_no": 6,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 269
        }
      ],
      "text": "She took a room above the chandler’s, where the window faced the marsh. Reeds ran out to the horizon and a single heron stood in them, patient as a fence post. By evening she had drawn the room, the stair, and the street as far as the pump, because drawing a place was the only way she knew of arriving in it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line_no": 7,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "line_no": 8,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 52
        },
        {
          "line_no": 9,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 102
        },
        {
          "line_no": 10,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 157
        },
        {
          "line_no": 11,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 204
        },
        {
          "line_no": 12,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 258
        },
        {
          "line_no": 13,
          "page": 8,
          "start_offset": 310
        }
      ],
      "text": "On the third day a boy came to the door and said he could carry things. His name was Tomás and he was eleven, or would be at Candlemas. His mother sold eels from a barrow and called every stranger señora regardless of evidence. Ada hired him for two pence a day and a share of whatever the marsh turned out to contain."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line_no": 1,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "line_no": 2,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 52
        },
        {
          "line_no": 3,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 107
        },
        {
          "line_no": 4,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 164
        },
        {
          "line_no": 5,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 220
        },
        {
          "line_no": 6,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 275
        },
        {
          "line_no": 7,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 330
        }
      ],
      "text": "They went out at first light with the chain and the poles. The boy walked ahead, testing the ground with a willow switch, and where the switch sank he said cuidado without turning round. By noon they had fixed forty-six stations and lost one boot. The wind brought salt, and under the salt the smell of something older, as if the sea had left its cellar door open."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line_no": 8,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "line_no": 9,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 52
        },
        {
          "line_no": 10,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 106
        },
        {
          "line_no": 11,
          "page": 9,
          "start_offset": 162
        }
      ],
      "text": "That night she inked the first sheet. She wrote Low Harbor in the corner and under it, smaller, the date, and then sat for a long while looking at the white part of the paper, which was most of it."
    },
    {
