        },
        {
          "line_no": 8,
          "page": 10,
          "start_offset": 273
        }
      ],
      "text": "It rained for five days. The marsh rose and took back the stations one by one, and Tomás counted them off from the window like a man reading names. On the sixth morning the water stood level with the chandler’s step and a pair of otters were seen in the high street, going about their business."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line_no": 9,
          "page": 10,
          "start_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "line_no": 10,
          "page": 10,
          "start_offset": 54
        },
        {
          "line_no": 11,
          "page": 10,
          "start_offset": 107
        },
        {
          "line_no": 12,
          "page": 10,
          "start_offset": 162
        },
        {
          "line_no": 13,
          "page": 10,
          "start_offset": 219
        },
        {
          "line_no": 1,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 269
        },
        {
          "line_no": 2,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 323
        }
      ],
      "text": "Osric Penn sent for her at noon. He had found, at the bottom of the biscuit tin, a map made by the drowned man: a single sheet, much folded, showing the marsh as it had been twenty years before. Every channel on it ran the wrong way. Ada turned it round twice and then understood that he had drawn north at the bottom, for reasons of his own."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line_no": 3,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "line_no": 4,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 56
        },
        {
          "line_no": 5,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 110
        },
        {
          "line_no": 6,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 167
        },
        {
          "line_no": 7,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 222
        },
        {
          "line_no": 8,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 273
        }
      ],
      "text": "She laid her sheet beside his. Where hers showed water, his showed a road lined with alder and a place called Saint Bride’s Acre, with a small cross to mark a chapel. Nobody in Low Harbor had heard of it. The harbormaster said the dead were entitled to their opinions, and poured the tea."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
