          "start_offset": 109
        },
        {
          "line_no": 12,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 165
        },
        {
          "line_no": 13,
          "page": 11,
          "start_offset": 220
        },
        {
          "line_no": 1,
          "page": 12,
          "start_offset": 273
        },
        {
          "line_no": 2,
          "page": 12,
          "start_offset": 330
        }
      ],
      "text": "Three weeks later the water went down. They walked out along the line of the drowned man’s road and found it under a hand’s depth of silt, cobbled, running straight toward nothing. The boy said camino, and then, because she was paying him, road. At the end of it stood the heron, or another like it, on a stone that had once been a step."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line_no": 3,
          "page": 12,
